      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "eslint.wording.config.js",
      "content": "The `.kind` exemption checks only `property.name`, so a computed access such as `result[kind] === 'MarkMissing'` is also exempt. Here `kind` can hold `'reason'`, allowing a prohibited reason-code comparison to pass both checks. Require a non-computed MemberExpression with property `kind` (including the optional-chain form) before exempting the operand.",
      "existing_code": "const notKind = (side) =\u003e wrapperPaths(side).map((p) =\u003e `:not([${p}.property.name=\"kind\"])`).join('');",
      "start_line": 87,
      "end_line": 87,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "eslint.wording.config.js",
      "content": "Optional chaining adds a `ChainExpression` layer, which consumes one of these traversal levels even though it is not a TypeScript wrapper. For example, `((status?.kind as string) satisfies string)! === 'AcknowledgedUnavailable'` has three supported wrappers but places the member access at depth four, so it is incorrectly rejected. Handle the chain layer separately from the three-wrapper budget and add a regression test for this permitted comparison.",
      "existing_code": "const wrapperPaths = (side) =\u003e [0, 1, 2, 3].map((depth) =\u003e `${side}${'.expression'.repeat(depth)}`);",
